00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:39.520
we start let's just cover the basics. what are&nbsp;
case studies? case studies are when you study an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:45.920
existing building or an existing project usually&nbsp;
a well-known piece of architecture to inform your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:52.240
design. if you want to design a chicken coop you&nbsp;
don't really want to start from scratch. you want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:58.640
to see how other people have done it, you want to&nbsp;
see how other people located their chicken coops,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:03.520
how they shaped it how they place the doors&nbsp;
and you want to learn from their mistakes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:09.280
